cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "GPIE — Green Policy Intelligence Engine: Independently Verifying Environmental Policy Claims Using Satellite Data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Maske"
    given-names: "Sakshi D."
repository-code: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/GPIE"
url: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/GPIE"
abstract: >-
  GPIE is a geospatial causal-inference framework that tests whether the European
  Climate Law (Regulation (EU) 2021/1119, effective 30 June 2021) produced a
  statistically distinguishable reduction in tropospheric NO2 pollution across the
  EU-27, using Sentinel-5P TROPOMI satellite observations (2019-2024) and a
  Difference-in-Differences causal-inference design with a genuine non-EU control
  group (United Kingdom, Norway, Switzerland). The corrected two-group model finds
  no statistically significant EU-specific effect (p = 0.663, cluster-robust
  standard errors), a result independently confirmed via a 23-quarter event-study
  analysis and a series of additional robustness checks. Applying the same design
  to a secondary NDVI (vegetation health) outcome finds a statistically significant
  relative decline (p = 0.012), reported as an exploratory finding.
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - difference-in-differences
  - satellite remote sensing
  - Sentinel-5P
  - air pollution
  - NO2
  - NDVI
  - European Green Deal
  - policy evaluation
  - geospatial analysis
